meta {
  name: Restart Attempt
  type: http
  seq: 31
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/assessments/attempts/{{assessmentAttemptId}}/restart
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
}

docs {
  Resets an assessment attempt back to a blank, freshly-started state —
  works from ANY status (completed, auto_submitted, terminated,
  under_evaluation, evaluated, result_published), not just a stuck
  in_progress one.

  What gets reset: every StudentAnswer row for this attempt is hard-deleted
  (a deliberate exception to this codebase's "soft deletes only" rule —
  answers are the literal content of a response being explicitly discarded
  by an authorized admin action, not a business record with its own
  lifecycle). The attempt itself goes back to status "in_progress" with a
  fresh started_at/last_activity_at (now), completed_at/total_score/
  max_score cleared to null, section_scores reset to {}, and
  anti_cheat_log cleared to [].

  Scope note: only the attempt is reset. The linked ApplicationCourse's
  pipeline status (e.g. "assessment_completed" if it was already
  evaluated/published) is deliberately left untouched — restarting does
  NOT revert it back to an earlier stage.

  404 if the attempt doesn't exist or belongs to a different college.
}
